     vveetthheerr — virtual Ethernet interface

SSYYNNOOPPSSIISS
     ppsseeuuddoo--ddeevviiccee vveetthheerr

DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The vveetthheerr interface simulates a normal Ethernet interface by encapsulat‐
     ing standard network frames with an Ethernet header, specifically for use
     as a member in a bridge(4).

     To use vveetthheerr the administrator needs to configure an address onto the
     interface so that packets can be routed to it.  An Ethernet header will
     be prepended and, if the vveetthheerr interface is a member of a bridge(4), the
     frame will show up there.

